Q: Color codes for tput setf A: <p>Using modern <a href="/questions/tagged/bash" class="s-tag post-tag" title="show questions tagged &#39;bash&#39;" aria-label="show questions tagged &#39;bash&#39;" rel="tag" aria-labelledby="tag-bash-tooltip-container" data-tag-menu-origin="Unknown">bash</a> with modern <a href="/questions/tagged/tput" class="s-tag post-tag" title="show questions tagged &#39;tput&#39;" aria-label="show questions tagged &#39;tput&#39;" rel="tag" aria-labelledby="tag-tput-tooltip-container" data-tag-menu-origin="Unknown">tput</a>, you could try something like:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>cmapDump () {
    local -a &quot;range=(seta{f,b}\ {0..${1:-7}}\ bel)&quot;;
    local cmap var=${range[*]};
    IFS= mapfile -td$'\a' cmap &lt; &lt;(tput ${var% bel});
    printf -v str '%%%%s %s\e[7m %%s.\e[0m\n' &quot;${range[@]% bel}&quot;;
    printf -v str &quot;$str&quot; &quot;${range[@]% bel}&quot;;
    printf &quot;$str&quot; &quot;${cmap[@]}&quot;
}
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li><code>$range</code> will hold an array of strings in form:  <code>&quot;setaf 0 bel&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;setaf 1 bel&quot;</code>.. <code>&quot;setaf X bel&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;setab 0 bel&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;setab 1 bel&quot;</code>.. <code>&quot;setab X bel&quot;</code>. Where X is either <code>7</code> or the argument submited.</li>
<li><code>$var</code> will host whole <code>$range</code> array into one string</li>
<li><code>$cmap</code> will parse output of <code>tput</code> by charactel <code>bell</code> (<code>0x07</code> or <code>\a</code>).</li>
<li><code>$str</code> host and construct a <em>format</em> string to print whole <code>$range</code> against whole <code>$cmap</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>(There are no loop!)</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>cmapDump
</code></pre>
